{
  "source": "09a8a14d",
  "experiment": "Generate exact immutable dense forward-L and L-transpose SSE2 programs, with constant workspace displacements, RIP-relative coefficient/WORK literals and original per-column predicates. Leave etas, input/output handling and all factor mutation outside. Main-agent implementation, Astra-high read-only opportunity review.",
  "configuration": "Pinned Rust1.98.1 ordinary ThinLTO release test binary/glibc/current EPYC host. Captured/small/initial replay probes unpinned. Final PILOT4/PEROLD direct-emitter replay pinned to CPU2. Not PGO, not a production solver benchmark.",
  "numerical_checks": "8192 complete SC50A captured dense passes (2factors x2directions x16MXCSR modes x128inputs): full-bit/random/signed-zero/exact-TOL/large/tiny/Inf/two-NaN-payload input patterns; every value bit, WORK bit and full MXCSR agrees with independent extracted original loops. Each of4888 actual initial-dense forward or dense-transpose passes captured in8 bounded solver runs also matches its live flat-kernel output/WORK/MXCSR exactly. All8 complete SolveResult Debug objects match separate uninstrumented same-binary solves. These do not constitute full candidate qualification for arbitrary inputs.",
  "emitter_revision": "Initial staging emitter builds code/data/relocations separately. Second emitter computes exact size and writes one mapped image in a single pass, without staging or relocation pass. Every one of182 observed geometry+direction images is byte-identical to the initial emitter. Both stages use RW mmap, then RX mprotect, then munmap on retirement. Original scalar-loop disassembly retained.",
  "replay_scope": "Eight fixed alternating AB/BA batches replay actual dense input histories. Candidate batch includes generation,mmap,mprotect,all uses and munmap; same input-copy cost included in both. Reference uses extracted original numeric loops over Vec columns, so it is not accepted-release timing attribution. Histories group all identical coefficients/geometry within a solve, an optimistic sharing assumption rather than proven per-factor lifetimes; capture/grouping costs and a production owner/cache are excluded. No failed sample is removed.",
